<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anthela</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anthela was a small place near the pass of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-thermopylae">Thermopylae</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, with a sanctuary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demeter">Demeter</a> Amphictyonis. It was the original meeting place of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delphic-amphictyony">Delphic Amphictyony</a>, the league of Greek peoples that later also met at Delphi, so that the council gathered at both sites each year.</p></div>
